---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SubNav from "../../components/SubNav.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Card from "../../components/Card.astro";
---

<Base title="The party — Party Dungeon" current="/mechanics/party/">
  <SubNav current="/mechanics/party/" />

  <header>
    <div class="kicker"><a href="/mechanics/">Mechanics</a> / The party</div>
    <h1>You build the party, not the character.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Classes carry their own skills. The interesting unit is the combination,
      not the individual.
    </p>
  </header>

  <Section title="The party">
    <div class="grid">
      <Card status="decided" title="Party building" tag="Yours">
        <p>
          Different <strong>classes</strong>, each with their own
          <strong>skills</strong>. Building the party is a core verb, not a
          character-select screen.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card status="guess" title="Why the party matters">
        <p>
          The fun comes from <strong>combinations</strong>: skills that set each
          other up, a party that is more than the sum of its classes. A player
          alone should feel incomplete.
        </p>
        <p>
          Which means the interesting failure is a <strong>bad party</strong>,
          not a bad player.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="What the party decides">
    <div class="grid">
      <Card href="/mechanics/crafting/" status="decided" title="Which disciplines you have" tag="Yours">
        <p>
          Smithing, cooking, and alchemy are held by classes. Your party
          composition decides what you can make &mdash; and what you have to
          buy.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
